Third-party components bundled in this repository
=================================================

This project is our own work. Two third-party, open-source components are
vendored or referenced; both are MIT-licensed and credited here. No MHD Flasher
code and no BMW SDK are included.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. MGU App Kit  (directory: kit/)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The build/runtime kit that every community MGU app uses: the Node runtime
(canvas, gauges, signals, display, fonts), the iDrive 8 boot/link layer, and the
build tooling (kit/tools/build.py and friends). Vendored unmodified so the app
builds and installs without an external checkout.

License: MIT. Full text: kit/LICENSE
  Copyright (c) 2026 cauliflowermossgrape
  Copyright (c) 2026 小白151 (GitHub: JackieZ123430) — Chinese translation

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. MHD live-monitor packed-block layout  (referenced in: apps/wali_datalog/mhdmonitor.js)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The field order and scaling of the UDS "2C 88 01" live-monitor block were
transcribed from the published ADX description used by the MIT-licensed
freebeamer/core project. Only the data-layout description is used; no code is
copied.

License: MIT (freebeamer/core).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Not included
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- BMW on-board SDK (oap-sdk) — supplied by the head unit at install time; a
  placeholder (oap-sdk/, git-ignored) stands in for local builds only.
- MHD Flasher application code — none is used.
